### Process Management Tests ###

# 1. Start the server with:
# npm run dev
#
# 2. Test graceful shutdown with different signals:
#    a. SIGTERM: kill -15 <PID>
#    b. SIGINT: Press Ctrl+C in terminal
#    c. SIGUSR2: kill -12 <PID>
#
# 3. Check logs for:
#    - Shutdown signal received
#    - Resource cleanup
#    - Server close
#    - Process exit
#
# 4. Verify database connections:
#    - Run health check before shutdown
#    - Try to make requests during shutdown
#    - Check database state after restart

### GraphQL User API Tests ###

### Query - Get All Users
POST http://localhost:3000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query { users { success users { id email name createdAt updatedAt } errors { field message } } }"
}

### Query - Get User by ID
POST http://localhost:3000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query($id: Int!) { user(id: $id) { success user { id email name createdAt updatedAt } errors { field message } } }",
  "variables": {
    "id": 2
  }
}

### Mutation - Create User
POST http://localhost:3000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation($input: CreateUserInput!) { createUser(input: $input) { success user { id email name createdAt updatedAt } errors { field message } } }",
  "variables": {
    "input": {
      "email": "test@example.com",
      "name": "Test User"
    }
  }
}

### Mutation - Create User with Invalid Email
POST http://localhost:3000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation($input: CreateUserInput!) { createUser(input: $input) { success user { id email name } errors { field message } } }",
  "variables": {
    "input": {
      "email": "invalid-email",
      "name": "Test User"
    }
  }
}

### Mutation - Update User
POST http://localhost:3000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation($id: Int!, $input: UpdateUserInput!) { updateUser(id: $id, input: $input) { success user { id email name } errors { field message } } }",
  "variables": {
    "id": 1,
    "input": {
      "name": "Updated Name"
    }
  }
}

### Mutation - Delete User
POST http://localhost:3000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation($id: Int!) { deleteUser(id: $id) { success errors { field message } } }",
  "variables": {
    "id": 2
  }
}

### GraphQL User API Tests ###

### Query - Get All Communities
POST http://localhost:3000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query Communities { communities { success communities { id name description influencer { id name email createdAt updatedAt } influencerId createdAt updatedAt } errors { field message } } }"
}

### Query - Get Community by ID
POST http://localhost:3000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query Community($id: Int!) { community(id: $id) { success community { id name description influencer { id name email createdAt updatedAt } influencerId createdAt updatedAt } errors { field message } } }",
  "variables": {
    "id": 1
  }
}

### Mutation - Create Community
POST http://localhost:3000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation CreateCommunity($input: CreateCommunityInput!) { createCommunity(input: $input) { success community { id name description influencer { id name email createdAt updatedAt } influencerId createdAt updatedAt } errors { field message } } }",
  "variables": {
    "input": {
      "name": "community init without description",
      "influencerId": 2,
      "description": null
    }
  }
}

### Mutation - Update Community
POST http://localhost:3000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation($id: Int!, $input: UpdateCommunityInput!) { updateCommunity(id: $id, input: $input) { success community { id name description influencer { id name email createdAt updatedAt } influencerId createdAt updatedAt } errors { field message } } }",
  "variables": {
    "id": 2,
    "input": {
      "name": "community but with updated description",
      "description": "new description"
    }
  }
}

### Mutation - Delete Community
POST http://localhost:3000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation($id: Int!) { deleteCommunity(id: $id) { success errors { field message } } }",
  "variables": {
    "id": 2
  }
}